<mxCell id="legend" value="&lt;b&gt;Sign-in&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font color=&#x27;#1f6fd1&#x27;&gt;■ blue, 1–10&lt;/font&gt; · &lt;b&gt;Update&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font color=&#x27;#d79b00&#x27;&gt;■ amber, A–F&lt;/font&gt; · &lt;b&gt;Provisioning and publishing&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font color=&#x27;#666666&#x27;&gt;- - grey&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;4 / B&lt;/b&gt;: MQTT over TLS with the key&#x27;s own certificate: presence requests up; Fleet commands down, responses up. &lt;b&gt;9&lt;/b&gt;: over the encrypted link the watch reads the challenge (“tinycrypt-presence-v1” ‖ nonce ‖ request hash) and writes its signature.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;E&lt;/b&gt;: an update waits 60 s for approval through steps 3–9 (“Install tinycrypt x.y.z?”), bound to SHA-256(“tinycrypt-ota-v1” ‖ image hash ‖ version); &lt;b&gt;F&lt;/b&gt;: write the spare slot, switch on approval, probation.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Presence is button OR watch&lt;/b&gt;; the button always works on its own. The push carries no authority: approval needs the watch&#x27;s Secure Enclave signature over a bonded BLE link, so the watch must be in range.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;The key is the trust anchor for updates&lt;/b&gt;: Fleet only triggers. An image installs only if its hash, signature and version pass and you approve it (bound to the image hash and version).&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Test only&lt;/b&gt;: the credential keys and the IoT private key sit in flash until the ATECC608 (CRYPT-22); secure boot and flash encryption are not yet enabled." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;spacing=8;rounded=1;strokeColor=#999999;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="750" width="880" height="150" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
</root>
</mxGraphModel>
</diagram>
</mxfile>
